+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The tool registry validates model-supplied input against each tool's declared JSON Schema before an executor can receive it.
+
+## Contract
+
+- A missing required property or a property with the wrong type returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failed schema constraint and does not invoke the executor ([validated by: returns a schema rejection for missing and wrongly typed fields without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L10)).
+- Valid input, including properties not listed in the schema, reaches the executor unchanged; an unregistered tool still throws its `Unknown tool` error ([validated by: passes valid input and unlisted properties through unchanged, and still throws for an unknown tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- A static schema is compiled at registration, so an uncompilable schema names its tool immediately and later mutation does not replace the compiled validator ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable schema at registration and compiles a static schema before later schema mutation](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved and validated against its current schema on every execution ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema resolved for each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L76)).
